### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 05 — HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP (HITL) GOVERNANCE & APPROVAL FLOW
###
### When an agent invokes a tool with operation = NETWORK_OUTBOUND
### and the session autonomy level is SUPERVISED (default), the
### ToolRegistry throws RequiresApprovalException instead of executing
### the tool. The AgentLoop saves the checkpoint as AWAITING_APPROVAL
### and returns a 202 response describing what needs approval.
###
### Two paths to approve/deny:
###   A) REST endpoints (tested here):
###        POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
###        POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/deny?agentRole=coordinator
###   B) Goal string in run/run-async (legacy path):
###        goal: "/approve"  or  goal: "/deny"
###
### Checkpoint states involved:
###   AWAITING_APPROVAL → agent paused, saved to SQLite
###   COMPLETED         → after successful approve + resume
###   FAILED            → after deny or approval timeout
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw serve mode, GROQ_API_KEY + GITHUB_TOKEN set
###   (GithubTool is NETWORK_OUTBOUND — the only tool that triggers HITL)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW A: REST APPROVE
# Create session → trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL → poll status → approve
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-1] Create session for approve flow
# @name approveSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-2] Run async — ask coordinator to use GitHub tool
# The GithubTool has ToolOperation=NETWORK_OUTBOUND + autonomy=SUPERVISED
# → ToolRegistry pauses execution and saves AWAITING_APPROVAL checkpoint
# Expect 202: {"toolName":"github","paramsJson":"{...}","sessionId":"..."}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-3] Poll status — should show AWAITING_APPROVAL
# Expect 200: {"sessionId":"...","status":"AWAITING_APPROVAL","steps":[...],"failReason":null}
# Run this immediately after HITL-2 before approving
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-4] APPROVE via dedicated REST endpoint
# agentRole query param (default: coordinator) must match the role in the checkpoint
# Expect 200: {"answer":"...","totalInputTokens":N,"totalOutputTokens":N}
# The agent resumes from the saved checkpoint with AutonomyLevel.FULL for this invocation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-5] Poll status after approve — should now be COMPLETED
# Expect 200: {"sessionId":"...","status":"COMPLETED","steps":[...],"failReason":null}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW B: REST DENY
# Create session → trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL → deny → check FAILED
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-6] Create session for deny flow
# @name denySession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-7] Run async — trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-9] Status after deny — should be FAILED
# Expect 200: {"sessionId":"...","status":"FAILED","steps":[...],"failReason":"Human denied via REST"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

### This always returns 200 if the key is valid — good for rate limit testing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

### [HITL-8] DENY via dedicated REST endpoint
# Expect 200: {"status":"DENIED","session":"..."}
# AgentSessionService.deny() calls agentStore.markFailed() and removes heartbeat
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/deny?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

### This always returns 200 if the key is valid — good for rate limit testing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW C: APPROVE VIA GOAL STRING (legacy in-band method)
# Sending goal="/approve" in run-async triggers the same approval path.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-10] Create session
# @name goalApproveSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-11] Trigger AWAITING_APPROVAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "View the rsrini7/arcclaw repository using the github tool.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-12] Approve via goal="/approve" in run-async
# AgentSessionService.runAsync() special-cases "/approve" → sets AutonomyLevel.FULL
# Expect: agent resumes and completes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [HITL-13] Deny via goal="/deny" in run-async
# Note: use on a DIFFERENT session that is AWAITING_APPROVAL
# AgentSessionService.runAsync() special-cases "/deny" → marks checkpoint FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/deny",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{goalApproveSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR / EDGE CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [HITL-14] Approve on non-existent session → expect 404 / CONFLICT
# AgentSessionService.approve() returns 409 CONFLICT if no AWAITING_APPROVAL checkpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-15] Approve on COMPLETED session → expect 409 CONFLICT (no pending approval)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [HITL-16] Approve without API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{approveSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

###

### [HITL-17] Deny without API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{denySession.response.body.sessionId}}/deny
Content-Type: application/json

###
